// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Heel Realization
// @category Character Development / Alignment
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Heel_Realization
// @domain   Mind
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): the moment a villain realizes they are the bad guy — confronted with the
// suffering they have caused, the Well-Intentioned Extremist who believed Utopia Justifies the Means
// suddenly sees themselves in the wrong. FRONTIER: the COGNITIVE precursor that Heel/Face Turn and the
// Redemption Arc build on. Those tropes flip the alignment and pay the debt; this is only the dawning
// self-directed recognition that lights them — guilt about what one DID and shame about who one IS,
// with no deed yet done. The realization is the seeing; the turn is the acting. A Knight Templar who
// DEFIES it never sees the wrong; a true believer who SUBVERTS it sees the pain and doubles down.


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/modules/emotion_dynamics.trl"     // appraises one's own deed -> self-directed guilt/shame

// Lateral thematic links (optional, machine-followable — for discovery / embeddings).
assoc heel_realization -> [
  heel_face_turn : "is the cognition whose deed is",
  redemption_arc : "lights the moral trajectory of",
  guilt          : "appraises the deed as",
  shame          : "appraises the self as",
  fall_from_grace : "is the moral waking its slide never reaches"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===
// The recognition is itself a beat of self-awareness — distinct from the Reversal it may precede.
imply HeelRealization -> [recognition, Conscience, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// A wrongdoer confronted with the harm of their OWN deeds appraises the self as the wrong — guilt for
// what they did, shame for who they are, the blame turned inward. This is the cognition ONLY: no
// defection, no atonement, no alignment flip — those belong to Heel/Face Turn and the Redemption Arc.
rule Heel_Realization {
  when:
    char $c [+Wrongdoer]
    evt  $mirror [&Confronts(target=$c)]
    not ( $c [+Zealous] )                   // a Knight Templar DEFIES it — never sees the wrong
  then:
    $c [#Guilty]                            // about what they DID
    $c [#Ashamed]                           // about who they ARE — the self-directed cut
    $c [~Blames(target=$c)]                 // the blame turns inward, not outward
    $c -- shame
}

// SUBVERTED: the true believer sees the same suffering and it only hardens the conviction — the pain
// is reframed as the price of the cause, and the realization curdles into resolve instead of remorse.
rule Heel_Realization_Subverted {
  when:
    char $c [+Wrongdoer] [+Zealous]
    evt  $mirror [&Confronts(target=$c)]
  then:
    $c [#Certain]
    $c -- conviction
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: A Song of Ice and Fire — Jaime Lannister's bath (novel/TV, 1996/2011) ===
// The Kingslayer, scorned for the oath he broke, finally tells the truth of it to Brienne in the
// baths of Harrenhal: he killed Aerys to spare half a million people from wildfire. But weak with
// fever, recounting his own life aloud, he hears what he has become — a man who pushed a child from a
// tower, who let the world's contempt make him careless and cruel. The confession is not the turn;
// he takes no vow, joins no side. It is the seeing — the moment the lion looks in the water and
// flinches. The deeds (riding back for Brienne, the honest steward of the realm) come after, and
// elsewhere.

// SER JAIME LANNISTER — "the Kingslayer," guarding a reputation he half-believes he deserves
char jaime [+Wrongdoer]

// BRIENNE OF TARTH — the mirror; her plain decency is what he measures himself against
char brienne [+Foil]

// INT. HARRENHAL BATHHOUSE - NIGHT — steam, fever, and the truth no one let him tell
set bathhouse [+Interior] [+Night]

scene the_confession {
  beat 1 {
    jaime @ bathhouse
    brienne @ bathhouse
    brienne -- jaime : "judges"
  }
  beat 2 {
    evt the_telling [&Confronts(target=jaime)]   // hearing his own life aloud, he sees what he is
    // Heel_Realization -> jaime [#Guilty] [#Ashamed] [~Blames(jaime)] -- shame
    // (NOT a turn: no [&Defects], no [+Ally]/[+Redeemed] — the deed comes later, in another scene)
  }
}
